			"notes": "Fixed an issue where some sword skills would fail when multiple players locked onto the same enemy.\nFixed an issue in multiplayer where the host could not lock onto enemies while holding another weapon or item, and pressing Z again would cancel the sword's lock-on.\n\nChanged sword skill activation for axes and other weapons: all sword skills can now be used except those that require right-clicking with a sword, such as Parry, Sword Break, and Helm Splitter, as well as Sword Beam.\nFixed an issue where the main-hand weapon's attack reach did not apply to attacks while locked on.\nAdjusted the base sword skill lock-on range.\nAdjusted and strengthened Dash Attack, Dodge, Flash Assault, Helm Splitter, Rising Cut, and Ground Slam.\n\nFixed music discs not playing any sound.\nImproved the song-playing experience and completed the song-learning advancement branch.\n\nFixed an issue with the Hookshot.\nAdjusted weapon and armor strength.\nReduced Darknut strength.\nAdjusted the strength and area of effect of the three elemental rods.\nAdjusted temple generation and key usage mechanics.\nAdded villager naming rules: villagers can be named after important NPCs, such as Zelda and Orca, to transform them into the corresponding NPC.\nCompleted the Skull Token reward progression.\n\nAdjusted Navi's entity behavior.\n\nReworked the Magic Mirror, allowing free travel between the Overworld and the Nether."
		}
